  "manual": {
    "notes": [
      "Not a direct ancestor (grand-uncle of Isaac J's line) but the family's most prominent 19th-century figure: youngest of John & Ann's ten children, b. 9 Jan 1816 in the 1743 homestead, d. 21 Apr 1880. Bought out his father's co-heirs; rebuilt/enlarged the house 1865 ('Built by Josiah Albertson 1743, rebuilt by Chalkley Albertson 1865'); m. Annie Stokes 1850; NJ Assembly 1863, '64, '67, '73; White Horse Turnpike incorporator; promoter of the Philadelphia & Atlantic City RR — the 'Albertson' locality north of Magnolia is named from his farm (RR stop arranged with Samuel Richards at his house, 1877). Sources: Prowell 1886 pp. 673-675; Biographical Review 1897; Magnolia borough history; HMDB markers."
    ]
  }
